---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A five-string electric violin built from 3D-printed parts, carbon-fiber reinforcement, and a piezoelectric pickup."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://rsms.me/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://rsms.me/inter/inter.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Five-String Electric Violin</title>
  </head>

  <body
    class="bg-[#0b1126] text-slate-200 selection:bg-[#aaccff] selection:text-[#113399]"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-screen-xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16 lg:py-0"
    >
      <div class="lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
        <header
          class="lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:flex lg:h-screen lg:w-[38%] lg:min-w-[360px] lg:flex-col lg:justify-center lg:py-16 mb-10"
        >
          <div
            class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-8 shadow-2xl shadow-blue-950/20 backdrop-blur"
          >
            <div
              class="absolute -right-20 -top-20 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 blur-3xl"
            >
            </div>

            <p
              class="mb-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Project Writeup
            </p>

            <h1
              class="mb-4 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
            >
              Five-String<br />Electric Violin
            </h1>

            <p class="max-w-sm text-base leading-7 text-slate-400">
              A 3D-printed five-string instrument built to extend the range of a
              violin and shape its sound electronically.
            </p>

            <nav class="mt-8 hidden lg:block">
              <div class="space-y-5">
                <a
                  href="#overview"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Overview
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#construction"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Build
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#electronics"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Electronics
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#iteration"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Iteration
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#experience"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Use
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#lessons"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Final Thoughts
                </a>

                <a
                  href="/projects"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#aaccff] transition hover:text-white"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-[#aaccff] transition-all group-hover:w-16"
                  ></span>
                  Return to Projects
                </a>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </header>

        <main class="w-full lg:w-[62%] lg:py-24">
          <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/violin-hero.png"
                alt="Fully assembled five-string electric violin"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                I started this project because I wanted to improvise below the
                range of a standard violin. After finding a five-string JAx
                Dragon Violin model, I decided to try building it myself.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                My first attempt failed when the hot-glue joints could not
                withstand the tension of even a single string. The second
                attempt used a much more substantial mechanical structure:
                printed PLA parts, M4 hardware, and a carbon-fiber rod running
                through the instrument.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="construction" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] md:items-center"
            >
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff] mb-6"
                >
                  Construction
                </h2>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The main fingerboard pieces were printed in black PLA and the
                  decorative frame in metallic teal PLA. A 300 mm carbon-fiber
                  rod provides internal structural support, while M4 nuts and
                  screws hold the printed sections together.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The result is a printed instrument that can actually carry the
                  mechanical load imposed by five strings.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <img
                  src="/images/violin-labeled.png"
                  alt="Labeled printed parts of the electric violin"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
                <img
                  src="/images/violin-exploded.png"
                  alt="Exploded view of the electric violin"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="electronics" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Electronics
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">01</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Tuning</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Guitar tuners replace typical violin pegs, providing a useful
                  balance between tuning range and control over intonation.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">02</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Pickup</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  A violin under-bridge piezoelectric pickup feeds a
                  preamplifier mounted beneath the guitar tuners.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <img
                src="/images/violin-tuners.png"
                alt="Guitar tuners and piezoelectric pickup"
                class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/violin-amp.png"
                alt="Guitar amplifier and Logitech speaker system"
                class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>

            <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
              For amplification, I tested several speakers before settling on a
              portable Logitech speaker system. A six-setting guitar amplifier
              provides control over volume and frequency ranges.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="iteration" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Iteration
            </h2>

            <div
              class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-7 sm:p-9"
            >
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                The first structural reinforcement was not long enough. After
                the fingerboard snapped at the end of the carbon-fiber rod, I
                measured the channel and determined that I needed roughly 380 mm
                of reinforcement. I purchased a 400 mm rod and cut it to size.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                I also found that one joint left the fingerboard slightly
                angled. A small hot-glue wedge corrected the angle and brought
                the playing surface back into alignment.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <img
                src="/images/violin-structure.png"
                alt="Carbon fiber rod through the central body of the violin"
                class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/violin-playing.png"
                alt="Playing the five-string electric violin"
                class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="experience" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              In use
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
              Because the electric violin conducts much less sound into my
              jawbone than an acoustic violin, I can hear something closer to
              what an audience hears. The amplifier also lets me directly shape
              the sound by adjusting specific frequency ranges.
            </p>
            <div
              class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/violin-playing-2.png"
                alt="Playing an arrangement for five-string violin"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="lessons" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16 pb-24">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Final Thoughts
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                This has become one of my favorite projects because it is
                responsive to what I do in the moment.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                Having a lower fifth string has expanded my improvisation into
                wider scales and deeper tones, and I have used the instrument to
                play arrangements such as Bach's Courante for five-string
                violin. I plan to continue creating my own musical instruments.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-white/10 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-600"
            >
              <span>Five-String Electric Violin</span>
              <a href="#overview" class="transition hover:text-slate-300"
                >Back to top ↑</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
